  - district heating
  - waste heat recovery
  - renewable energy integration
abstract: >-
  Mixed-Integer Linear Programming model for optimal co-sizing of Battery
  Energy Storage Systems (BESS) and Borehole Thermal Energy Storage (BTES)
  integrated with an AI data center on a modified IEEE 14-bus Arctic
  distribution grid in Narvik, Northern Norway. The model jointly optimizes
  electrical and thermal energy management considering wind, hydro, grid
  purchase, heat pump, and waste heat recovery.
